-- title:
--   Uniqueness of finite predictable measures from adapted generating rectangles
-- statement:
--   Let two measures be defined on the predictable sigma-algebra generated by an adapted filtration's initial-time and strict-future past-event rectangles. If the first measure is finite and the two measures agree on every {bottom}×A with A measurable at time bottom and every (t,infinity)×A with A measurable at time t, then the two measures coincide on all predictable events. This is a non-circular monotone-class extension of elementary rectangle compensation; the rectangle identities remain to be established from the actual Poisson point measure, and no general Campbell identity is assumed.
-- source:
--   Pinned Mathlib 0df444a360eaa60ab8c11dca51a86af692955474, Mathlib/Probability/Process/Predictable.lean (Filtration.predictable generators) and Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Measure/Restrict.lean (Measure.ext_of_generateFrom_of_iUnion). Applebaum, Levy Processes and Stochastic Calculus, 2nd ed., marked Poisson integration.

